# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# cad-arr2026 — what is NOT tracked, and why.
#
# Rule of thumb (experiment-discipline, version-control-for-experiments.md):
#   track code, configs, the ledger, measured configuration, and primary evidence;
#   ignore regenerable caches and anything large that a re-run reproduces exactly.
# Every negated (re-included) pattern below carries its reason. Do not delete one
# without reading it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Python / OS -----------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.DS_Store
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
venv/

# --- Secrets: NEVER commit --------------------------------------------------
# HF tokens and judge API keys are passed through the environment on the pod.
.env
.env.*
*.key
*secret*
*token*.txt
.huggingface/

# pod_pull.sh parks files here while it pulls; per-pull scratch, never evidence.
.pull_aside/

# --- LaTeX build products (Overleaf rebuilds them) -------------------------
paper_arr2026/*.aux
paper_arr2026/*.bbl
paper_arr2026/*.blg
paper_arr2026/*.log
paper_arr2026/*.out
paper_arr2026/*.synctex.gz
paper_arr2026/*.fdb_latexmk
paper_arr2026/*.fls

# --- Pod scratch output ----------------------------------------------------
# Runners write here while they run. These are IGNORED on purpose: git never
# touches ignored files, so a `git pull` on the pod can never overwrite a
# half-finished run. Results that the paper cites are copied into results/
# and committed from the laptop, which is the durable machine.
rtsd_fullres_checkpoints/
pincer_k40_checkpoints/
controls_checkpoints/
gemma_generation_checkpoints/
qwen_generation_checkpoints/
leace_checkpoints/
e1_outputs/

# Large tensors are regenerable from the model and too big for history.
*.pt
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.npz

# EXCEPTION — the loudness filter norms (17 KB).
# This file DEFINES which 2,083 of the 4,164 AccessEval pairs are used. It is a
# measurement, not a cache: runners that cannot find it RECOMPUTE it, and a
# recomputation can move the median by one tie, which is how one earlier run got
# a 2,082-pair pool and another 2,083. Three copies because three runners look in
# three places; all three are byte-identical (sha256 checked at commit time).
angular_checkpoints/*
!angular_checkpoints/accesseval_loudness.npz
baseline_results/*
!baseline_results/caa_checkpoints/
!baseline_results/angular_checkpoints/
baseline_results/caa_checkpoints/*
baseline_results/angular_checkpoints/*
!baseline_results/caa_checkpoints/accesseval_loudness.npz
!baseline_results/angular_checkpoints/accesseval_loudness.npz

# --- results/ is TRACKED ---------------------------------------------------
# Primary evidence. Generation uses do_sample=True, so re-running produces
# DIFFERENT text: these files cannot be regenerated, only reproduced in
# distribution. The paper quotes specific responses from them. The CAD
# per-response texts from the first frontier sweep were lost this way (left on
# a pod that was shut down); only their judge scores survived.
# Nothing to ignore here; listed so nobody adds results/ above by accident.
